---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PageIntro from "../components/PageIntro.astro";
import { source } from "../lib/links";
const categories = [
  ["Exploits", "42,748"],
  ["Fuzzers", "33,816"],
  ["Generic", "19,651"],
  ["Reconnaissance", "17,074"],
  ["DoS", "5,980"],
  ["Backdoor", "4,659"],
  ["Shellcode", "2,381"],
  ["Analysis", "1,226"],
  ["Worms", "158"],
];
---

<Layout
  title="Dataset"
  description="NF-UNSW-NB15-v3 provenance, schema, distribution, quality and preprocessing."
  section="Dataset"
>
  <PageIntro
    eyebrow="02 / Data provenance"
    current="Dataset"
    title="NF-UNSW-NB15-v3, examined at the source."
    description="The dataset is an evidence source, not an operational traffic feed. The repository records the publisher, checksums, raw schema, observed quality issues and the conditions for model use."
  />
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="facts">
        <div>
          <small>Publisher</small><strong>University of Queensland</strong>
        </div><div>
          <small>Stable record</small><strong
            ><a href="https://doi.org/10.48610/6E0EDA1"
              >DOI 10.48610/6E0EDA1 ↗</a
            ></strong
          >
        </div><div>
          <small>Verified CSV</small><strong>2,365,424 rows · 55 columns</strong
          >
        </div><div>
          <small>License</small><strong>Commercial use restricted</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section rule">
    <div class="container two-column">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Population</span><h2>
          A heavily imbalanced flow record.
        </h2><p class="lede">
          The verified CSV contains 2,237,731 benign flows and 127,693 attack
          flows. These are counts in this package, not estimates of real-world
          traffic prevalence.
        </p><div
          class="distribution"
          role="img"
          aria-label="Dataset distribution: 94.6 percent benign and 5.4 percent attack"
        >
          <span style="width:94.6%"></span><span style="width:5.4%"></span>
        </div><div class="legend">
          <span>● Benign · 2,237,731</span><span>● Attack · 127,693</span>
        </div><p class="note">
          The publisher landing-page attack total differs by 54 rows from the
          verified CSV. This portal follows the checked file bytes. <a
            href={source("docs/dataset/NF_UNSW_NB15_V3_PROVENANCE.md")}
            >Read discrepancy record ↗</a
          >
        </p>
      </div><div class="surface category-panel">
        <h3>Attack categories</h3><div class="table-wrap">
          <table class="data-table">
            <caption class="sr-only"
              >Attack category counts in verified CSV</caption
            ><thead
              ><tr><th scope="col">Category</th><th scope="col">Rows</th></tr
              ></thead
            ><tbody
              >{
                categories.map(([name, count]) => (
                  <tr>
                    <>
                      <th scope="row">{name}</th>
                      <td>{count}</td>
                    </>
                  </tr>
                ))
              }</tbody
            >
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Data contract</span><h2>
        55 raw columns, three distinct roles.
      </h2><div class="schema-grid">
        <div class="surface">
          <span class="schema-num">47</span><h3>Model features</h3><p>
            Ordered NetFlow attributes such as protocol, byte and packet counts,
            timing, TTL and flow statistics. Numeric-coded categories remain
            distinct from quantitative fields.
          </p>
        </div><div class="surface">
          <span class="schema-num">06</span><h3>Trace metadata</h3><p>
            Start/end timestamps, source/destination IPv4 addresses and both L4
            ports are retained for grouping and trace context, but excluded from
            baseline <code>X</code>.
          </p>
        </div><div class="surface">
          <span class="schema-num">02</span><h3>Targets</h3><p>
            <code>Label</code> is binary (0 benign, 1 attack); <code
              >Attack</code
            > contains Benign or one of nine attack categories. Both are excluded
            from input features.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div><p class="source-line">
        The baseline retains the publisher's NetFlow v3 flow statistics in a
        fixed order. No additional selected-feature set or 49-feature port
        variant is presented as an evaluated model.
      </p><p class="source-line">
        Source: <a href={source("docs/dataset/NF_UNSW_NB15_V3_SCHEMA.md")}
          >verified schema ↗</a
        > · <a href={source("src/network_anomaly/data/nf_unsw_nb15_v3.py")}
          >executable feature contract ↗</a
        >
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section rule tinted">
    <div class="container two-column">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Acquisition and quality</span><h2>
          Checked before transformation.
        </h2><p>
          The fetch script obtains a short-lived URL from UQRDM, verifies
          archive and payload checksums, and keeps the large CSV outside Git.
          The streaming validator checks row width, schema, labels, missing and
          non-finite tokens, and duplicate fingerprints.
        </p><div class="callout">
          The raw quality record reports blank and positive-infinity rate
          values, exact duplicates and equivalent flow vectors. A successful
          source-integrity check is not a statement that raw data is directly
          ML-ready.
        </div><p class="source-line">
          <a href={source("scripts/fetch_nf_unsw_nb15_v3.py")}
            >Acquisition code ↗</a
          > · <a
            href={source(
              "reports/data_quality/nf_unsw_nb15_v3_validation.json",
            )}>Quality report ↗</a
          >
        </p>
      </div><div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Split and preprocessing</span><h2>
          Fit only on Train.
        </h2><ol class="steps">
          <li>
            <strong>Partition</strong><span
              >Chronological, group-aware Train / Validation / Test with purge
              gaps.</span
            >
          </li><li>
            <strong>Audit</strong><span
              >Record exact and feature-equivalent vectors; targets and trace
              metadata stay outside <code>X</code>.</span
            >
          </li><li>
            <strong>Transform</strong><span
              >Map missing/non-finite values to missing sentinels, then use
              train-derived medians or modes. Validation and Test receive frozen
              transforms.</span
            >
          </li><li>
            <strong>Evaluate</strong><span
              >Use Validation for development and preserve Test for a separately
              reported final check.</span
            >
          </li>
        </ol><p class="source-line">
          <a href={source("reports/splits/nf_unsw_nb15_v3_split_manifest.json")}
            >Split manifest ↗</a
          > · <a href={source("docs/NF_UNSW_NB15_V3_PREPROCESSING_POLICY.md")}
            >Preprocessing policy ↗</a
          >
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container two-column">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Reproducibility</span><h2>
          Use the official record.
        </h2><p>
          Follow repository instructions to fetch and validate the package. The
          SHA-256 pins in the manifest were computed by the project from
          official bytes; they are not publisher-authored SHA-256 values.
        </p><a class="button" href={source("docs/DATASET.md")}
          >Dataset guide ↗</a
        >
      </div><div class="surface license-note">
        <h3>Attribution and licensing</h3><p>
          The dataset is under UQ's “Permitted Re-Use with Commercial Use
          Restriction” terms, requiring full citation and non-commercial use.
          The repository's Apache-2.0 source license does not relicense the
          data.
        </p><a href="https://doi.org/10.48610/6E0EDA1">Publisher record ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
<style>
  .facts {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .facts > div {
    padding: 1rem;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .facts > div:first-child {
    padding-left: 0;
  }
  .facts > div:last-child {
    border: 0;
  }
  .facts small,
  .facts strong {
    display: block;
  }
  .facts small {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .facts strong {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }
  .two-column {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 5rem;
  }
  .two-column h2 {
    margin: 0.7rem 0 1rem;
  }
  .two-column p {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .distribution {
    display: flex;
    height: 20px;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: 2px;
    margin: 2rem 0 0.6rem;
  }
  .distribution span:first-child {
    background: var(--cyan);
  }
  .distribution span:last-child {
    background: var(--violet);
  }
  .legend {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
  }
  .legend span:first-child {
    color: var(--cyan);
  }
  .legend span:last-child {
    color: var(--violet);
  }
  .note {
    font-size: 0.84rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }
  .note a,
  .source-line a,
  .license-note a {
    color: var(--cyan);
  }
  .category-panel {
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }
  .category-panel h3 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .category-panel .data-table {
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .category-panel td {
    text-align: right;
  }
  .schema-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }
  .schema-grid > div {
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }
  .schema-num {
    font-size: 2.1rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--cyan);
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
  }
  .schema-grid h3 {
    margin: 0.8rem 0;
  }
  .schema-grid p {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }
  .source-line {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .tinted {
    background: var(--surface);
  }
  .steps {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .steps li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 100px 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding: 1rem 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  .steps strong {
    color: var(--cyan);
  }
  .license-note {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    align-self: start;
  }
  .license-note h3 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .license-note p {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .facts,
    .schema-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
    .two-column {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 3rem;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 550px) {
    .facts,
    .schema-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .facts > div {
      padding: 1rem 0;
      border-right: 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    }
    .facts > div:last-child {
      border: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
